# Doc-driven workflow
## Hierarchy
| Level | What | Artifact |
|---|---|---|
| Epic | big business goal | wiki `Epic-<Name>` + parent issue |
| Feature | demonstrable, checkable result | wiki `Feature-<Name>` + issue; links its epic |
| Subtask | small work item | issue only; links `Feature-<Name>#<anchor>` |
- Subtask needing own analysis -> promote to feature. Bugs/small fixes: issue with criteria, then steps 5-7. Closed work: no new docs.
- Page sections: «Бизнес и сценарии», «Архитектура», «Решения», «Разбиение», «Тест-кейсы». Templates: wiki `Epic-Template`, `Feature-Template`.
- `<Name>`: Latin, English, Title-Case-With-Hyphens; not renamed casually.
## Steps (one step = one owner; a step starts only when the previous one is on the page)
| # | Rule | Step | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `playbook-step-01-analysis.mdc` | Бизнес и сценарии | analyst |
| 2 | `playbook-step-02-architecture.mdc` | Архитектура + Разбиение | architect |
| 3 | `playbook-step-03-decisions.mdc` | Решения | analyst <-> architect -> lead -> owner |
| 4 | `playbook-step-04-test-cases.mdc` | Тест-кейсы, BEFORE code | tester |
| 5 | `playbook-step-05-development.mdc` | code | developer |
| 6 | `playbook-step-06-review.mdc` | review + security | architect + devops |
| 7 | `playbook-step-07-acceptance.mdc` | acceptance on dev | tester |
| 8 | `playbook-step-08-docs.mdc` | Doc-/ADR after merge | analyst + architect |
## Common
- Issue = control panel (status label + page link). Artifacts on the wiki page, not in chat; a comment only announces a filled step.
- Fill only your section. Disagreement -> step 3.
- Cloud agent executor: give it this file + the step file; it returns ready section text (or a PR); the launcher reviews, publishes, comments.
